NHINRL, but it'd be funny trying to imagine that one, wouldn't it?

Based on weight, you'd either have glass the density of tempered steel, 
(in which case, how the heck does it break when dropped?!) or reeaally 
dense liquid (you quaff the potion of speed.  The potion of speed 
perforates your stomach!)  Or, normal density glass, normal density 
liquid, just a gallon of it, per potion.  (You quaff the potion of full 
healing.  Pestilence polishes its claws.  --more--  Pestilence whistles 
tunelessly.  Pestilence shuffles its feet.  --more-- You feel completely 
healed!)

Based on quaffing speed, and breakability, it's probably about the 
volume of a shot glass, in something like a beaker with a stopper on it. 
  The encumbrance isn't only weight, though.  It's also the amount of 
difficulty required to lug the thing around without spilling, or 
breaking it.  The more glass you carry, the more likely you are to be 
moving slowly so as not to trip and shatter something.  </rationalization>

